**Company Description**

Launched in 2021 with a simple yet bold mission, Flink set out to give people back their most valuable resource: time. We didn't just join the quick commerce race, we defined its potential. By enabling customers to order from a curated selection of over 3,000 groceries and household essentials through our user-centric app, we deliver what people need in minutes. We have fundamentally shifted the retail landscape across Germany and the Netherlands, while embedding sustainability into our core through an all-electric delivery fleet, recyclable packaging, and a focus on reducing food waste.

Today, Flink has evolved from a disruptive startup into a resilient and sustainable powerhouse. In an industry defined by rapid change, we’ve mastered the balance of hyper-efficiency and massive scale. With a network of around 160 hubs, we now bring the Flink experience to more than 22 million people, making us an integral part of the urban infrastructure. This impact is driven by a dedicated team of more than 10,000 colleagues, including a fully employed rider fleet that serves as the backbone of our operations. By generating over €550m in revenue in 2025, we have proven that our model is not only desirable but financially formidable.

Having built a proven foundation, we are now shifting from establishing our presence to accelerating our impact. Backed by prestigious partners like Prosus, Mubadala, Bond, DoorDash, Btomorrow Ventures and REWE, and fueled by fresh investment, we are entering our next major growth phase. We are thinking bigger, expanding our footprint, and refining every link in our value chain.  

Our culture is defined by a shared bias for action and the commitment to being 1% better every day. We take ownership, stay close to the frontline, and support one another to ensure we never let another Flinker fail. We celebrate diversity and believe that our multicultural team is our greatest competitive advantage.  

Are you ready to shape the future of quick commerce with us?

 **Job Description**

We're looking for a proactive and detail-oriented Working Student to join our HQ People Team. You'll play a crucial role in supporting the smooth day-to-day operations of our department and have the opportunity to contribute your own ideas and energy to our projects.

* **Support Daily Operations:** Assist with administrative tasks, including managing employee files, and supporting our onboarding and offboarding processes;
* **Manage Employee Data:** Accurately input and maintain employee data using our HRIS (Human Resources Information System) and other internal platforms;
* **First Point of Contact:** Serve as the initial point of contact for employee inquiries regarding company policies, benefits, and administrative processes via our internal ticketing system;
* **Contribute to Documentation:** Help create and maintain essential internal documentation, such as our employee handbook and departmental guides, ensuring all information is accurate and up to date;
* **Support Special Projects:** Collaborate with team members on ad-hoc projects aimed at enhancing the overall employee experience. This could involve supporting culture building initiatives, organising team events, or contributing to our Talent Management strategy.


**Qualifications**  

* Currently enrolled as a student pursuing a degree in Human Resources, Organizational Psychology, Business Administration, or have experience in a related field; prior experience in a similar administrative or people-focused role is also a plus;
* Ability to learn and work with HR tools and platforms effectively and proficiency in Google Workspace;
* Strong attention to detail, stakeholder, and time management skills;
* Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;
* Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion;
* Eagerness to learn and contribute in a collaborative team environment;
* Availability to work at least 16 hours per week during regular business hours;
* Proficiency in German and English.


**Additional Information**

For this role as Working Student - People Team (m/f/d), the starting remuneration is as follows:

The base pay for this position is 14.00 - 16.00 EUR gross for full time (20 hours per week).

* A €1000 annual L&D budget as well as individual coaching options to ensure you have plenty of opportunities to learn, grow and achieve your goals
* 26 days of vacation, +1 day every year up to a maximum of 30 days
* A mobility budget of 35 EUR per month for Deutschland Ticket subsidy
* A discount on your Urban Sports Club membership
* Bike leasing through JobRad
* Attractive company pension options
* Unlimited access to an e-learning and development platform, Prosus Academy, including online German courses
* Online discounts with Corporate Benefits and Future Bens
* A cool discount off your personal Flink orders; be the first to test out new products!
* A modern and dog-friendly office in the heart of Berlin - lots of delicious lunch spots available within short walking distance

*It is our commitment that every applicant will be evaluated according to their skills regardless of age, gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability status, or religion.*

#### **We are looking for**

**Student Research Assistant (f/m/d)**
--------------------------------------

(part-time - up to 20 hours per week)


to start in November 2026. The **Behavior** **Research Program** at ISDC focuses on how people, households and groups cope with major shocks to lives and livelihoods. We study how experiencing these shocks shapes choices, preferences and coping strategies, and contributes to wellbeing at the individual and household levels, as well as how they aggregate through society as a whole.

#### **Your responsibilities**

* Conducting literature reviews;
* Managing and cleaning large, complicated data sets;
* Supporting the analysis micro-level data using econometric techniques; and
* Contributing to the drafting of project publications.

#### **We think you’d be a great fit if you**

* Are currently enrolled as a student in a Master’s degree program in economics, agricultural economics, nutrition, data science, or a related discipline in the wider Berlin area;
* Have experience in cleaning large datasets and conducting statistical / econometric analysis in Stata and/or R;
* Have a demonstrated topical interest in studying conflict, development, behavior, and/or humanitarian policy;
* Have done impact evaluation; and
* Are capable of fluently communicating and writing in English.

#### **What you’ll gain by working with us**

* Work on pressing global challenges with interesting donors, partners, and networks;
* The possibility to be part of (and learn from) a diverse, international team of researchers;
* A 12-month contract, with the possibility of extension, working up to 20 hours per week;
* A salary of 15,08 Euro gross per hour;
* Flexible work model; including the opportunity to work remotely from abroad for 3 weeks per year;
* 30 days of annual leave (full-time equivalent) and additional days off additional days off on 24 and 31 of December; and
* An exciting and collaborative working environment in a modern office space near S+U Wedding station.

#### **Interested?**

Then we encourage you to apply! Please upload your CV, relevant transcripts, and a short cover letter (maximum one page) explaining why you would be a great fit for this position via the respective fields in the application portal. Examples of any relevant work samples are beneficial, but not mandatory. The deadline for applications is 10 November 2026. Please note that applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and that the position may be filled before the application deadline. We ask that applicants kindly refrain from follow-up questions after application and strive to get back to every applicant as soon as possible.  

We are looking forward to hearing from you!

#### **About us**

**ISDC – International Security and Development Center** is a non-profit academic institute based in Berlin, Germany. We believe in the power of data to study the impact of violent conflict, humanitarian emergencies, and fragility on lives and livelihoods. You can find out more about us and our work by visiting www.isdc.org.
